Better: assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null => \result[i] == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\result[i]));

But note precedence: && lower than =>? Actually => lower priority than &&, so we need parentheses: (this.get(i) == null => \result[i] == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\result[i]))

Wrap inside forall: \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null => \result[i] == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\result[i]))

That's the assert.

